From 18a454b0db4520b79d720059cd572cbcc2f3e572 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:35:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gemini): --provider gemini without -m uses a Gemini
 model; aux default gemini-3.8-flash [daveey]

--provider X without -m kept the config's model, so a claude-* default went to Gemini and
404'd on every call. A model that clearly belongs to another vendor on a single-vendor
provider (gemini, anthropic) now falls back to that provider's default; explicit -m and
unknown ids are untouched. Gemini's aux default (title generation etc.) and the native
adapter's default model move to gemini-3.8-flash, the id Google points new keys at
(gemini-2.5-* 404s 'no longer available to new users').
---
